text:
jamie: FYI ran into a frustrating TS/ESM edge case while onboarding a user on Vercel Edge. Our TS generics vanish for one public API after the bundling step. Repro: https://github.com/redwood/repro-edge-esm-types.

ashley: can you show the minimal function that regresses?

jamie: yep. sdk surface:
```ts
// src/api.ts
export function request<T>(payload: T): Promise<{ value: T }>;
export function request(payload: unknown) { return Promise.resolve({ value: payload as any }); }
```
consumer:
```ts
import { request } from '@redwood/sdk';

type P = { x: number };
async function main(){
  const out = await request<P>({ x: 1 });
  // Expect out.value to be P. In ESM edge bundle it's any (no completions)
  out.value.
}
```

kevin: does the CJS build keep the overloads?

jamie: yes. cjs dist/index.d.ts shows the overloads. dist/esm/index.d.ts shows a single widened signature (payload: any).

maria: packaging config? exports map? tsconfig?

jamie: package.json exports:
{".": {"import": "dist/esm/index.js","require": "dist/cjs/index.js"}}

tsconfig uses module: esnext, moduleResolution: bundler, declaration: true, emitDeclarationOnly: true. We use esbuild to bundle ESM entry that re-exports internals: `export * from './runtime'`.

ashley: i think rollup/esbuild can rewrite the esm entry in a way that collates declarations and loses overload relationships. If the wrapper is the only file the declaration emitter sees, it might get a merged signature.

kevin: short-term: tell users to import the cjs entry or pin until we fix. Long-term: preserve .d.ts for esm entry (generate single index.d.ts with explicit overloads) or change packaging to point import to the original compiled file with its d.ts.

maria: also check if typesVersions in package.json is present and pointing at wrong path. I've seen TS pick the wrong file in presence of an exports map and types field.

jamie: good point. our types field points to dist/types/index.d.ts which is generated by running tsc only against src (not the wrapper). But the published tarball has a generated dist/esm/index.d.ts produced by the bundler step that overwrote it.

packager-bot: Created ticket ENG-5207: "ESM packaging step collapses SDK generic overloads for Edge consumers". Attached repro and initial diff of d.ts.

kevin: plan: 1) add CI that compares public API surface between cjs & esm builds (emit declarations and run a structural diff), 2) make esm packaging avoid re-export wrapper or ensure bundler preserves overload declarations, 3) if needed ship a hand-crafted index.d.ts for stability.

ashley: i'll add a small consumer test (vercel edge sample) to our mono repo that pulls the package tarball and types-checks. That should catch regressions.

maria: i'll update SDK README with a troubleshooting note and the deep-import workaround: `import { request } from '@redwood/sdk/dist/cjs'` until ship fix. Also mention tsconfig flags to look for.

jamie: thanks. i'll post PR with CI job and try the direct types entry change. cheers.
